##
## `PACK_NAME product` resolves because the shipped root is non-empty on this branch.
## Commit your bundle under `E/descriptors/<producer>/<bundle>/` **before** splicing
## this call, or the registered census will run against a shard that does not contain
## your descriptors.
##
## The call registers one CTest entry per arch the `product` pack target was wired
## with: hip-kernel-provider-hkp-census-<arch>-Test{{ config.engine.pascal_name }}Packs.
## It runs hip_kernel_provider_tests --gtest_filter=Test{{ config.engine.pascal_name }}Packs.*
## with HIPDNN_TEST_CENSUS_SUITE=Test{{ config.engine.pascal_name }}Packs,
## HIPDNN_TEST_EXPECTED_ARCH=<arch> and HIPDNN_DESCRIPTOR_DIR set to that pack
## target's own out-root shard for <arch>, under the labels
## unit_test;hip-kernel-provider;host. A suite name may be declared at one pack
## target only -- the CTest name carries no pack component, so a second declaration
## is a configure error rather than a rename.
## Every registered case must execute and pass without skipping in every iteration.
## Missing suites, filtered/disabled/sharded-out cases and zero iterations fail.
##
## EXPECTED_CASES arrives as HIPDNN_TEST_CENSUS_EXPECTED_CASES, comma-separated, and
## pins this suite's case-name set. Execution alone cannot catch a suite that SHRINKS:
## the obligation set is built from the registered cases, so a case that stops being
## compiled takes its own obligation with it and the census still reports complete. The
## pin is compared by name in both directions -- expected-but-unregistered and
## registered-but-unexpected each fail, because a count lets the two cancel. Regenerate
## and re-splice this call whenever the bundle's shape changes: has_heuristic,
## is_multi_pack and behavior_notes each add or remove a case, and the list above is
## read straight out of the suite this run rendered, so it already reflects them.
## The call also registers a control per arch whose pin names a case that does not exist
## and which must emit the lost-a-case diagnostic to pass, which is what proves the
## comparison is still live.
